A Syrian court on Tuesday sentenced former ruler Bashar al-Assad to death after a trial in absentia, convicting him of atrocities committed during the country's civil war. Six of his closest aides were also handed death sentences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73c8abca-956f-11f1-aff4-e70fbbb452ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:58:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg">AFP - LOUAI BESHARA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and EU join international aid effort after Colombia earthquake</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-france-eu-join-international-aid-effort-after-colombia-earthquake</link><description>
France has joined the European Union and a host of countries in offering assistance to Colombia, where volunteers and rescuers are searching for survivors following Monday's deadly earthquake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e96a684-955e-11f1-bebd-75c492606bc4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:08:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg">© Jamie Saldarriaga / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran says ‘Muslim Nato’ pact reflects retreat from US security umbrella</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-iran-says-muslim-nato-pact-reflects-retreat-from-us-security-umbrella</link><description>
Tehran has played down concerns over a new mutual defence pact between Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan, while portraying the agreement as evidence of declining regional reliance on the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">505d03ae-94b9-11f1-840e-457ddd2c08ca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:21:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Record temperatures swept regions home to 900 million people in July</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-record-temperatures-swept-regions-home-to-900-million-people-in-july</link><description>
Regions home to around 900 million people experienced their hottest July on record in 2026, including areas in the Sahel, Central America, France and Spain, according to analysis of Copernicus data.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13fd717a-949e-11f1-84b4-d34b2a11c752</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:33:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg">© Ina FASSBENDER / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Moscow and Damascus reach deal over Russian military bases in Syria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-moscow-and-damascus-reach-deal-over-russian-military-bases-in-syria</link><description>
Syria said on Sunday it had reached a deal with Moscow on the fate of Russia's two bases in the country, which it once used to provide military support to ousted leader Bashar al-Assad during the Syrian civil war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67a3afc4-9476-11f1-b20d-ffc054c909af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 04:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG">REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Netanyahu rejects Gaza plan in new break from Trump</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260809-netanyahu-rejects-gaza-plan-in-new-break-from-trump</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Sunday rejected a US-led Gaza plan endorsed by Hamas, putting distance between himself and President Donald Trump as he tries to shore up his base ahead of close elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ac69f26-93f2-11f1-862d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e9706596eee8ad4dc033e95d5a1ada753b3e6111.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ac69f26-93f2-11f1-862d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e9706596eee8ad4dc033e95d5a1ada753b3e6111.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b6eeeec-93f2-11f1-85c5-771bd1b13781</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 13:00:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ac69f26-93f2-11f1-862d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e9706596eee8ad4dc033e95d5a1ada753b3e6111.jpg">© Omar AL-QATTAA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Sall's chances at UN secretary-general role weakened after first vote</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260809-sall-s-chances-at-un-secretary-general-role-weakened-after-first-vote</link><description>
Antonio Guterres’s successor as United Nations secretary-general will be named in October. So far, two candidates from the African continent – Senegal’s Macky Sall and Uganda’s Olara Otunnu – have failed to win sufficient support.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d4af0a0-8cca-11f1-913c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-23T212854Z-1702020119-RC2XJMADDLIE-RTRMADP-3-UN-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d4af0a0-8cca-11f1-913c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-23T212854Z-1702020119-RC2XJMADDLIE-RTRMADP-3-UN-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b068822-90b8-11f1-a55e-290a92cb9c17</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 07:35:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d4af0a0-8cca-11f1-913c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-23T212854Z-1702020119-RC2XJMADDLIE-RTRMADP-3-UN-ELECTION.jpg">© Eduardo Munoz/ Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Spain begins border checks on travellers from Italy amid migration showdown</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260808-spain-begins-border-checks-on-travellers-from-italy-amid-migration-showdown-europe</link><description>
Spain on Saturday began temporary border checks on travellers from Italy in response to Rome imposing similar measures at the end of July, after a mass migrant rush into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/75edd264-90c3-11f1-b2fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26214317437629.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/75edd264-90c3-11f1-b2fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26214317437629.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8dedb9b4-9330-11f1-b07c-b9f5e1fc00ab</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 15:41:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/75edd264-90c3-11f1-b2fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26214317437629.jpg">AP Photo/Antonio Sempere - Antonio Sempere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Turkey's new opposition party offers hope, but its future is already in jeopardy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260808-turkey-s-new-opposition-party-offers-hope-but-its-future-is-already-in-jeopardy</link><description>
The launch of the Yeni Party in Turkey promises to energise the country's struggling opposition. But while some polls show it leading, it remains vulnerable – already beset by arrests it says are "politically motivated". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4b81e0c8-5eab-11f1-affd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/TURQUIE-OZGUR-OZEL-PARLEMENT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4b81e0c8-5eab-11f1-affd-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/TURQUIE-OZGUR-OZEL-PARLEMENT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4d9894a-9230-11f1-9dba-e3260db61049</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 10:20:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>High stakes for Ireland's EU presidency amid migration row over Ceuta crisis</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260808-high-stakes-for-ireland-s-eu-presidency-amid-migration-row-over-ceuta-crisis</link><description>
Ireland this week found itself at the centre of Europe’s increasingly fraught migration debate, as it sought to calm a dispute among European Union member states following last week's influx of 50,000 people into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c623b36a-5a16-11ef-a5ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34TD726.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c623b36a-5a16-11ef-a5ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34TD726.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ba6c5f4-9187-11f1-8912-fd507ef24b37</guid><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 07:34:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c623b36a-5a16-11ef-a5ad-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34TD726.jpg">© AFP/Ben Stansall</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>The EU has new anti-Beijing instruments, but will China have to face the music?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260807-the-eu-has-new-anti-beijing-instruments-but-will-china-have-to-face-the-music</link><description>
When Western companies rushed into China in the 1980s and 1990s, they traded their latest technology for market access. Now, China has absorbed, adapted and improved foreign know-how and is flooding Europe with advanced products, while the European Union's trade deficit balloons. As Paris and Berlin finally align on a response, analysts question whether Brussels' defensive "instruments" can contain a rival it helped create.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b598fc2-6b02-11f1-97cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6PG2PF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b598fc2-6b02-11f1-97cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6PG2PF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a422fd2-9172-11f1-a419-8d27d6502f9b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 20:05:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b598fc2-6b02-11f1-97cf-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6PG2PF.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Rwanda in talks with Italy to take in migrants trying to reach EU</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260807-rwanda-in-talks-with-italy-to-take-in-migrants-trying-to-reach-eu</link><description>
Days after Italy proposed setting up a network of migrant reception centres outside the European Union, Rwanda has confirmed that it is in talks with the Italian government about potentially hosting people seeking asylum in the EU.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb3157d0-dadc-11ec-8fa4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32AG8D7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb3157d0-dadc-11ec-8fa4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32AG8D7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa626000-9244-11f1-8c80-c9b100b5e473</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:01:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb3157d0-dadc-11ec-8fa4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32AG8D7.jpg">© AFP - SIMON WOHLFAHRT </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Russia accuses France of ‘silencing dissent’ over journalist expulsion</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260806-russia-accuses-france-of-silencing-dissent-over-journalist-expulsion</link><description>
Russia has accused France of suppressing freedom of expression, after French authorities ordered the expulsion of pro-Kremlin Russian journalist Xenia Fedorova and froze her assets.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69ebb164-8f3f-11f1-9540-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18015482650134.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69ebb164-8f3f-11f1-9540-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18015482650134.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bde345b6-9192-11f1-ab20-e135b2d0c4c5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 15:15:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69ebb164-8f3f-11f1-9540-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18015482650134.jpg">AP - Francois Mori</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Why has Ukraine's former military chief given up on NATO membership?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260805-why-has-ukraine-s-former-military-chief-given-up-on-nato-membership</link><description>
The former chief of Ukraine's armed forces, Valery Zaluzhny, says his country, fighting Russian invasion since 2022, will "never" join NATO – despite Kyiv's intention to become a member of the military alliance. While some analysts suggest Zaluzhny is primarily seeking to highlight the alliance’s weaknesses, others say he is laying the groundwork for a presidential bid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/93be3d60-9037-11f1-b2e1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25036570432104.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/93be3d60-9037-11f1-b2e1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25036570432104.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec19a994-90ce-11f1-b044-95452f6a71c6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 18:54:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/93be3d60-9037-11f1-b2e1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25036570432104.jpg">AP - Efrem Lukatsky</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Jordan warns status quo in Jerusalem 'under threat' as ministers meet in Amman</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260805-jordan-warns-status-quo-in-jerusalem-under-threat-as-ministers-meet-in-amman</link><description>
Amman hosted an emergency ministerial meeting on Wednesday to rally support behind Jordan’s custodianship of Jerusalem’s holy sites, as Foreign Minister Ayman Safadi warned that Israeli measures risk igniting a wider religious conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/20492c38-4fc7-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ISRAEL-JERUSALEM-MARCHE-DRAPEAUX-14MAI2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/20492c38-4fc7-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ISRAEL-JERUSALEM-MARCHE-DRAPEAUX-14MAI2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6d802474-90be-11f1-989c-6f8594e3bf55</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 15:07:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/20492c38-4fc7-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ISRAEL-JERUSALEM-MARCHE-DRAPEAUX-14MAI2026.jpg">AP Photo/Leo Correa - Leo Correa</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France announces further investment to combat drug trafficking in Guiana</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260805-france-announces-further-investment-to-combat-drug-trafficking-in-guiana</link><description>
France's Minister for Public Accounts outlined on Monday a slew of measures designed to combat drug trafficking in the Caribbean territory of French Guiana, one of the world's major hubs for smugglers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/207515aa-109f-11ea-8b9e-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1cs3o3_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/207515aa-109f-11ea-8b9e-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1cs3o3_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50a3dbf2-9005-11f1-953c-63f11d1765e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 08:54:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/207515aa-109f-11ea-8b9e-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/000_1cs3o3_0.jpg">jody amiet / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Kremlin critic leaves Moscow for Paris after ban from running for election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260805-kremlin-critic-leaves-moscow-for-paris-after-ban-from-running-for-election</link><description>
Russian anti-war politician Boris Nadezhdin has left the country after being prevented from standing in September’s parliamentary elections, becoming the latest prominent Kremlin critic to move abroad amid an intensifying crackdown on dissent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f86556b0-8fe0-11f1-971f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2FB468.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f86556b0-8fe0-11f1-971f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2FB468.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f61fbd0-8fdd-11f1-80f1-75c61b62a88b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 06:06:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f86556b0-8fe0-11f1-971f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2FB468.jpg">AFP - ALEXANDER NEMENOV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Seventh round of talks between Lebanon and Israel under way in Rome</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260804-seventh-round-of-talks-between-lebanon-and-israel-under-way-in-rome</link><description>
Lebanon and Israel began a new round of United States-sponsored direct talks in Rome on Tuesday, as Beirut seeks Israel's phased withdrawal from the country's south. But critics, including Hezbollah, say the talks amount to a "surrender" by Lebanon. 
